{"name":"Dragon Bay","hex":"#5da99f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dragon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical reptilian or serpentine creature.","In European mythologies, a gigantic beast, typically reptilian with leathery bat-like wings, lion-like claws, scaly skin and a lizard-like body, often a monster with fiery breath."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of drag queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dragon Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Dragon Bay is a natural bay in Newfoundland, Canada. Indrafts include Mooring Cove, Willis Cove, Tickle Cove, and Crew Cove. Dragon bay runs in a westerly direction for more than 3 miles (4.8 km) from the entrance to Facheux Bay. It is narrow and deep throughout, with no anchorage. The south point of the entrance to this bay is Red Rock, the north point is Gray Rock, which has a cave. Little Hole lies 0.75 miles (1.21 km) west of Dragon Bay, and has shelter for small vessels."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Bay","wikidata":"Q5305165"},{"title":"Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"A dragon is a mythical creature found in the folklore of cultures throughout the world. It is roughly serpentine in form, and often possesses features drawn from different animals, such as wings and claws. In nearly all cultures, it is conceived of as a powerful and awe-inspiring creature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png/330px-St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon","wikidata":"Q7559"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ivan_Bilibin_065_%28frameless%29.jpg/330px-Ivan_Bilibin_065_%28frameless%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ivan_Bilibin_065_%28frameless%29.jpg/330px-Ivan_Bilibin_065_%28frameless%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam